          "type": "string",
          "attribute": "disable",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "''",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "string",
            "resolved": "string",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Comma-separated feature flags to disable. Recognised values:\n - `ai`   — skip the Ollama probe, omit AiBlock + AiInlineTool tools.\n - `task` — omit TaskBlock + the `[ ]` paragraph→task auto-conversion.\n\nUse from tasks-app where the editor is a plain note pane (no AI, no\ncross-collection task creation): `<pop-editor disable=\"ai,task\" ... />`."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
          "name": "wikilinks",
          "type": "boolean",
          "attribute": "wikilinks",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "false",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "boolean",
            "resolved": "boolean",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Opt-in: enable the `[[wiki-link]]` inline tool (notes-app Phase 3). When on,\ntyping `[[` opens a note-title autocomplete and inserts an inline link chip\ncarrying the target noteId. The autocomplete + lazy-create resolve through\nhost-provided globals (`window.__notesLinkSearch` / `__notesLinkCreate` /\n`__notesLinkNavigate`) so ui-kit stays decoupled from notes-app's data layer.\nOff by default — the main app's editor is unaffected."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
          "name": "assistantSlash",
          "type": "boolean",
          "attribute": "assistant-slash",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "false",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "boolean",
            "resolved": "boolean",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Opt-in: add an \"Ask the Assistant\" entry to the slash / block \"+\" menu\n(notes-app WS3). Selecting it does NOT insert a block — it dispatches a\n`notes-app:open-assistant` window event (verb `build`) that the host app's\nunified Assistant (WS2) listens for, then removes its own placeholder block.\nThis reuses the SAME invocation path as the selection toolbar (no second\nassistant). Off by default so other pop-editor hosts are unaffected."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
